<title>USA: BOXING-MOSLEY WINS IBF LIGHTWEIGHT TITLE.</title>
<headline>BOXING-MOSLEY WINS IBF LIGHTWEIGHT TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>UNCASVILLE, Connecticut 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Shane Mosley won a unanimous points decision on Saturday to take the International Boxing Federation lightweight title from South African Phillip Holiday on Saturday.</p>
<p>The judges scored the fight 116-113, 117-111 and 115-114 for the new champion.</p>
<p>Mosley raised his record to 24-0, while Holiday suffered his first defeat to fall to 31-1.</p>
